{"type": "message", "id": "9c6669a0", "parentId": "78500bef", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T05:35:10.663Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_233a5f3ab1d14f089d4ada5a", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"\\\"2022 NAEP\\\" grade 8 math Kansas score\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 862,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6bd234883a5ef287\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6bd234883a5ef287\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a1fcf818cfdf64bd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAmong the states/jurisdictions with score declines, <strong>18 scored lower than the national average score for public school students in 2022</strong>; 16 had average scores that were not significantly different from the national public average; and 17 scored higher. Explore detailed state average score results ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a1fcf818cfdf64bd\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a36b894f5aab438e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nProficiency plummets to historic lows on 2022 NAEP in Kansas - Kansas Policy Institute\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a36b894f5aab438e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://kansaspolicy.org/proficiency-plummets-to-historic-lows-on-2022-naep-in-kansas/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e8339445e6c55f9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n#41 in 8th-grade math for low-income students. The eight-score composite (average of all scores) gives Kansas a national rank of <strong>#36</strong>. The top five states are Massachusetts, Florida, Mississippi, Indiana, and Wyoming.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e8339445e6c55f9\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"November 1, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"kansaspolicy.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e1d86b4cd9b41e1f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n72% of Kansas 8th Graders Aren’t Proficient in Math | Aligned\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e1d86b4cd9b41e1f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.wearealigned.org/blogs/72-kansas-8th-graders-arent-proficient-math\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a0b528e543058fdc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAccording to the 2022 NAEP (Nation’s Report Card): 72% of Kansas 8th graders are below proficient in math. Kansas’s <strong>average 8th-grade score: 274</strong>, which is slightly above the national average, but far from top-performing states.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a0b528e543058fdc\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 1, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.wearealigned.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6aa69e333b9fbadc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExplore Results for the 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6aa69e333b9fbadc\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"56fcd67a98f91035\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAverage scores at grades 4 and 8 were higher compared to the first assessment in 1990. Download a summary of the 2022 mathematics results. ... More detailed mathematics assessment results are available throughout this Report Card. ... The NAEP mathematics assessment measures students&#x27; knowledge and skills in mathematics and students&#x27; ability to apply their knowledge in problem-solving situations.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"56fcd67a98f91035\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7de02a07244e1b50\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nKansas 2022 NAEP reading, math results drop in Nation’s Report Card\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7de02a07244e1b50\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cjonline.com/story/news/education/2022/10/25/kansas-2022-naep-reading-math-results-drop-nations-report-card/69580903007/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"acabe7e01019af04\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn Kansas, the decline in fourth-grade math scores similarly dropped four points, but the eighth-grade decline was more pronounced, <strong>dropping 10 points to levels not seen since 2000.</strong>\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"acabe7e01019af04\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 25, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cjonline.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "\"2022 NAEP\" grade 8 math Kansas score", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 862, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6bd234883a5ef287\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6bd234883a5ef287\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a1fcf818cfdf64bd\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAmong the states/jurisdictions with score declines, <strong>18 scored lower than the national average score for public school students in 2022</strong>; 16 had average scores that were not significantly different from the national public average; and 17 scored higher. Explore detailed state average score results ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a1fcf818cfdf64bd\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a36b894f5aab438e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nProficiency plummets to historic lows on 2022 NAEP in Kansas - Kansas Policy Institute\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a36b894f5aab438e\">>>", "url": "https://kansaspolicy.org/proficiency-plummets-to-historic-lows-on-2022-naep-in-kansas/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8e8339445e6c55f9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n#41 in 8th-grade math for low-income students. The eight-score composite (average of all scores) gives Kansas a national rank of <strong>#36</strong>. The top five states are Massachusetts, Florida, Mississippi, Indiana, and Wyoming.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8e8339445e6c55f9\">>>", "published": "November 1, 2022", "siteName": "kansaspolicy.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e1d86b4cd9b41e1f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n72% of Kansas 8th Graders Aren’t Proficient in Math | Aligned\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e1d86b4cd9b41e1f\">>>", "url": "https://www.wearealigned.org/blogs/72-kansas-8th-graders-arent-proficient-math", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a0b528e543058fdc\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAccording to the 2022 NAEP (Nation’s Report Card): 72% of Kansas 8th graders are below proficient in math. Kansas’s <strong>average 8th-grade score: 274</strong>, which is slightly above the national average, but far from top-performing states.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a0b528e543058fdc\">>>", "published": "August 1, 2025", "siteName": "www.wearealigned.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6aa69e333b9fbadc\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nExplore Results for the 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6aa69e333b9fbadc\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathema